 ## Changelog
+- 2026-10-16: LoD rework: real chunks become the LoD (Voxy's ingest, `voxy_worldgen_v2` as the reference). Written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; run `cargo test --lib --release lod` first (`a_tree_is_leaves_over_its_own_ground`, `a_tree_meshes_as_a_box_on_a_trunk`, `an_ingested_chunk_replaces_the_guess` are new; `a_cell_keeps_...` and `a_tile_meshes_...` changed).
+    - Why it looked buggy (video + screenshots): (1) a column was only its top block, so a tree was a pillar from the top leaf to the lawn with a trunk-coloured wall, and at coarse steps a 16 x 16 pillar; (2) the LoD was a second opinion of the generator: no edits, populate order not the ring's, no trees beyond 300 blocks, and it showed a guess over chunks that were already loaded (the ring draws 4 chunks, 7 stay loaded). Why it felt choppy: the index buffer was re-created for every near tile each time the eye moved 2 blocks, even when the set of covered cells had not changed.
+    - Ingest: `ChunkManager::settle_around` (after a populate lands, a populate runs, or a saved chunk loads) hands a chunk over once all four populates that write into it are done (`settled`); on unload it is handed over again if it had been (edits). `take_ingest` -> `Lod::ingest` -> worker `Store::ingest` (kept in `Store::real`, laid over its tile now and in every tile made later, pruned beyond 48 chunks). The tiles it touches (and neighbours, for edge walls) are meshed again `REMESH_WAIT` = 2 s after the first chunk of a burst (Voxy's `ChunkUpdateTracker` throttle). Replaces `take_unloaded` / `far::columns`; `world/far.rs` and `lod/` stay in the tree, unused.
+    - Voxy map: `ChunkGenerationManager` + `DistanceGraph.findWork` = `Store::make` asked nearest-first (`want`, `MAX_PENDING`); `VoxelIngestService.ingestChunk` = `Lod::ingest`; `ChunkUpdateTracker` = `dirty` + `REMESH_WAIT`. Not ported: `ChunkPersistence` (completed-chunk save), so the guessed tiles are generated again each run.
+    - Trees: `Col` gained `leaf` / `lb` / `lmeta` / `ltint` / `log`; `column` reads through trunk and air to the ground; `build` draws the ground normally plus a leaf box (top, bottom, sides minus what the neighbouring crown hides) and a trunk at step 1; `resolve` keeps a forest cell's mass at the mean crown height (a quarter of the cell under leaves) and drops a lone tree. `TREES` 300 -> 520, `KEEP_TILES` 900 -> 700.
+    - Cut: `indices` split into `covered` + `gather`; `Tile::cut` makes a new index buffer only when `covered` changed.
+    - ponytail: no persistence; trunk only at step 1; edits far from the player only show once their chunk loaded; one worker; `TREES` 520 makes ~3x the generate + populate work of 300 (36 chunks per tile with its margin), first fill on a phone may take minutes (lower `TREES` if so). UNVERIFIED: that it compiles, speed and memory on a device, the look of the leaf boxes.
 - 2026-10-16: MERGE of `Repo.zip` (Voxel LoD, Voxy style) and `Repo-merged.zip` (Tectonic, Nether, title screen, light thread, lazy noise, height-column distant terrain). Written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run. The common base was recovered by reversing `voxel-lod.patch` on `Repo.zip`; a three-way merge then left only the two LoD systems in conflict (`lib.rs`, README, ROADMAP); `mesh.rs` and `chunks.rs` merged cleanly.
     - Both replaced the same smooth heightfield LoD. The Voxel LoD is the one `App` draws: `App.lod: Option<Lod>` (was `far`), made by `new_lod` wherever the chunk manager is made (`reset_world`, `enter`; `Lod::new(self.seed, self.tectonic)`), none in the Nether, dropped by `quit_to_title`, drawn where `far` was, `camera.zfar = lod::ZFAR` (256 without it), fog ends at `lod::RADIUS`. `take_unloaded` is still drained and dropped (the Voxel LoD does not ingest real chunks; no persistence, so `far`'s `<world>/far` save call is gone).
     - Kept, not wired: the `lod/` crate and `world/far.rs` (`chunks.rs` still fills `unloaded` with `far::columns`, `camera.rs` still takes its initial `zfar` from `far::FAR_BLOCKS`). To go back to them: restore the `far` field, `new_far`, the `save` / `draw` / `update` calls and the fog line from the Repo-merged.zip `lib.rs`. UNVERIFIED: that `world/lod.rs` compiles against the merged generator (`OverworldGenerator::{new, tectonic, generate, populate}`, `WorldChunkManager::new`, `Region::new` are unchanged by the merged patches), run `cargo test -p tectonic -p embeddium -p lod` and `cargo test --lib --release` first.

